<td id="S2.T1.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S2.T1.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">age</span>, <span id="S2.T1.5.6.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sex</span>, <span id="S2.T1.5.6.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weight</span>, <span id="S2.T1.5.6.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">serum_creatinine</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.T1.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.5.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Calculates creatinine clearance using the Cockcroft–Gault equation based on the given parameters.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Dataset</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From cases discussed at ICT meetings in 2024, we identified eight patients who had received vancomycin for MRSA bacteremia. To ensure clinical relevance and applicability in ICT, we defined six tasks (Table <a href="#S2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 2.3 Dataset ‣ 2 Methods ‣ EHR-MCP: Real-world Evaluation of Clinical Information Retrieval by Large Language Models via Model Context Protocol" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). These were categorized into two levels: Simple tasks (<span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">culture_history</span>, <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">body_weight</span>, <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lab_data</span>, <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">antibiotics</span>), which could be completed with a single tool call, and Complex tasks (<span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">calculate_ccr</span>, <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">culture_negative</span>), which required multi-step tool use and reasoning. Depending on the task, the data retrieval window was set either to the day of intervention initiation or to a one-month period before and after the intervention. Gold-standard answers for each task were prepared by physicians, who manually extracted and formatted the required information from the EHR.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each task, prompts were prepared in both English and Japanese. They included placeholders for patient ID and the data retrieval period, and examples of the required output format were provided in JSON. Because access restrictions prevented automated retrieval of sex and age that were required for calculating creatinine clearance, these values were manually extracted and embedded into the prompts as placeholders. Details of each task, including the actual prompts, are provided in the Supplementary.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Tasks and Expected Tool Calls</span></figcaption>
